# Verify before done

Before saying a task is **done**, run checks for the parts of the repo you changed.

## Required when

Non-trivial code: auth, API routes, Drizzle schema, middleware, pages, docker/deploy.

## Skip when

Typo in comment/docs only, single sentence in `.mdc` / README with no behavior change.

When unsure — run the checks.

## Minimum (oval)

| Touched | Before reporting |
|---------|------------------|
| `app/**`, `lib/**`, `middleware.ts` | `pnpm run task -- validate` (or lint + build) |
| `lib/training/**`, `lib/payments/**` | + `pnpm run test:unit`; if DB behavior changed → `pnpm run task -- test-integration` |
| `app/api/webhooks/**`, `app/api/test/**` | `pnpm run task -- test-integration` |
| `lib/db/schema/**`, auth plugins | `pnpm run auth:generate` if Better Auth config changed; `pnpm run db:generate` if hand-edited schema; `pnpm run task -- db-migrate` or document why not |
| `.docker/**`, `scripts/task.ts`, `.env.example` | Smoke: `pnpm run task -- dev-up` if stack changed |
| `tests/**` | Run the suite you changed (unit / integration / e2e) |

Optional before merge: `pnpm run task -- validate-full` or `pnpm run task -- test-all`. E2E: `pnpm run task -- test-e2e` (Docker + Playwright).

## Reporting

1. Fix failed lint/test/build first; only then say “done”.
2. Note which commands you ran.
3. Do not commit unless the user explicitly asks.
